I’ll treat the day-21 vaccination campaign as occurring before most post-day-20 transmission. Vaccination cuts the effective susceptible pool sharply: about half of the 3,871 remaining susceptibles are vaccinated, leaving an initial “effective susceptible” pool of roughly \(0.5 + 0.05 \times 0.5 = 52.5\%\) of susceptibles, or about 2,030 fully-susceptible-equivalents. With 911 currently infectious, incidence should initially remain substantial but fall as remaining unvaccinated susceptibles are depleted.

My forecast median is around 1.1k new infections by day 40, with moderate stochastic spread.

